-- title:
--   Fourier transform of the Cesaro core
-- statement:
--   For every natural $M$ and real $t$ with $\sin(\pi t)\ne0$, the Fourier transform of the differentiated Cesaro core equals its finite averaged trigonometric expression: the Fejer triangle factor multiplies the cotangent main term and the mean of the oscillatory terms $\pi it\,i\cos(\pi(2N+1)t)/\sin(\pi t)$ for $N<M$. Division by $M$ follows Lean's convention also at $M=0$.
-- source:
--   Supporting lemma in the explicit Beurling-Selberg argument, following J. D. Vaaler, Some extremal functions in Fourier analysis, Bulletin of the AMS 12 (1985), Section 2. Original Lean source: MathExtras/NumberTheory/Analysis/VaalerCesaroFTPieces.lean, lines 317-363.

